    "content": "Kampala, September 19, 2026 — Uganda's People's Defence Forces (UPDF) announced the immediate suspension of all defense and military cooperation with the Republic of Turkey, according to a statement released by acting Defense Information Spokesperson Colonel Chris Magezi. The decision took effect at once and will remain in place until outstanding issues related to the two countries' defense and military partnership are resolved.\n\nThe UPDF statement did not specify the nature of the issues that prompted the suspension, nor did it provide a timeline for when the situation might be reviewed. Colonel Magezi's announcement offered no further details about which specific programs or agreements fall under the suspension. Turkey has not yet issued a public response to the Ugandan decision.\n\nUganda and Turkey have maintained defense ties in recent years, with Turkish military equipment and training programs featuring in Uganda's security procurement. Turkey has expanded its defense footprint across Africa over the past decade, supplying drones, armored vehicles, and training support to several governments in the region. The suspension marks a notable interruption in that relationship.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, the development carries indirect significance. Turkey is a major security partner for Somalia, training elite units of the Somali National Army and providing significant development assistance. Any shift in Turkey's military engagements in East Africa can affect regional security calculations, including those connected to the fight against al-Shabaab and the African Union transition mission. Uganda likewise contributes troops to that mission, making its defense partnerships relevant to Somalia's stability.\n\nThe suspension also arrives amid a broader pattern of changing alliances in the Horn of Africa and East Africa. Somali diaspora communities across Uganda, Turkey, and the wider region often follow such developments closely, given their business, family, and remittance ties spanning these countries. Analysts will be watching for further statements from Kampala or Ankara that clarify the reasons behind the decision and its potential duration.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/09/19/uganda-oo-hakisay-dhammaan-iskaashigii-milatari-ee-ay-la-lahayd-turkiga/",
